    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Can we replace \r\n\r\n```js\r\nif (typeof additionalQueryParameters === 'function') {\r\n  const queryLanguages = language\r\n    ? [language.split('-')[0]]\r\n    : undefined;\r\n  helper.setState(\r\n    helper.state.setQueryParameters({\r\n      queryLanguages,\r\n      ignorePlurals: true,\r\n      removeStopWords: true,\r\n      optionalWords: query,\r\n      ...additionalQueryParameters({ query }),\r\n    })\r\n  );\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nwith something like\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst queryLanguages = language\r\n  ? [language.split('-')[0]]\r\n  : undefined;\r\n\r\nif (typeof queryLanguages !== 'undefined' || typeof additionalQueryParameters === 'function') {\r\n  helper.setState(\r\n    helper.state.setQueryParameters({\r\n      queryLanguages,\r\n      ...(typeof additionalQueryParameters === 'function' && {\r\n        ignorePlurals: true,\r\n        removeStopWords: true,\r\n        optionalWords: query,\r\n        ...additionalQueryParameters({ query }),\r\n      })\r\n    })\r\n  )\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nSince `language` is a widget param, user should be able to use it without having to use `additionalQueryParameters`. I don't know how to make it prettier, though.",
